Package: mzLibR
Title: R Bindings for the mzLib Proteomics Library
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Michael R.", "Shortreed", email = "mshort@chem.wisc.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-4626-0863"))
Description: Calls the mzLib proteomics library from R over a language-neutral
    bridge: reading mass-spectrometry data files ('mzML', Thermo '.raw',
    Bruker '.d', timsTOF, MGF and msalign), spectral libraries ('.msl') and
    the result files of a dozen search tools, retention-time calibration
    onto a library's iRT scale, SDRF-Proteomics
    experimental-design files (label-free and isobaric designs), protein
    databases ('UniProt' XML, FASTA) with 'Ensembl' gene resolution,
    sequence alignment, 'Ensembl Compara' orthology and residue mapping
    across species, PRIDE repository
    access with checksums, in-silico digestion and fragmentation of
    peptidoforms, conversion of full sequences to 'Unimod' and 'ProForma'
    notation, label-free quantification with match-between-runs via
    FlashLFQ, Gene Ontology annotation of protein groups, and the moderated
    t-test of 'limma' with contrasts, Benjamini-Hochberg adjustment,
    random-effects meta-analysis, p-value combination, Spearman correlation,
    logistic and mixed models per feature (also on a latent scale, from
    measured and counted samples), entrapment false discovery
    estimates, design matrices from sample sheets, and PTM site occupancy as
    mzLib computes them. The bridge is a self-contained executable that
    carries its own .NET runtime, so no .NET installation is required. It is
    shared with the Python ('pyMzLib') and Rust ('mzLibRust') bindings,
    which means all three agree field for field.
